Manage access keys: additional credentials of a user (service accounts), with an
optional expiration and an optional inline policy that restricts what the
key can do (the permissions are the intersection with those of the user).

Usage:
  nexoctl admin accesskey [flags]
  nexoctl admin accesskey [command]

Aliases:
  accesskey, access-key, svcacct

Available Commands:
  create      Create an access key (the secret key is printed only once)
  edit        Change an access key: secret, status, expiration, inline policy
  info        Show an access key (never its secret)
  list        List access keys (of the user of the alias, or of --user)
  remove      Remove access keys (their requests fail immediately)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for accesskey

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin accesskey [command] --help" for more information about a command.
